00:12:23.000 --> 00:12:24.000
and all these other things,

00:12:24.000 --> 00:12:26.000
and we're constantly observing everything that's around us,

00:12:26.000 --> 00:12:28.000
but we don't take the time to really observe

00:12:28.000 --> 00:12:30.000
what's going on inside of ourselves.

00:12:30.000 --> 00:12:32.000
And that's what meditation is for me.

00:12:32.000 --> 00:12:34.000
Habit number five,

00:12:34.000 --> 00:12:36.000
change your environment with Ed Milet.

00:12:36.000 --> 00:12:38.000
I had read all the books on personal development.

00:12:38.000 --> 00:12:40.000
I learned about influence,

00:12:40.000 --> 00:12:42.000
kind of learned how to change my state,

00:12:42.000 --> 00:12:43.000
how to think differently.

00:12:43.000 --> 00:12:45.000
I've been to a lot of the events that you go to.

00:12:45.000 --> 00:12:47.000
Why is it that so many people go to all these

00:12:47.000 --> 00:12:49.000
self-improvement, personal development, business events?

00:12:49.000 --> 00:12:51.000
They get all excited when they're there,

00:12:51.000 --> 00:12:52.000
they're ready to conquer the world.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:53.000
Then they get back home,

00:12:53.000 --> 00:12:56.000
and life very slowly starts to drift back to normal.

00:12:56.000 --> 00:12:58.000
And that's because environment overrides

00:12:58.000 --> 00:13:00.000
almost everything in our lives.

00:13:00.000 --> 00:13:01.000
That's why.

00:13:01.000 --> 00:13:03.000
And so the reason you're so excited

00:13:03.000 --> 00:13:04.000
when you're at the event,

00:13:04.000 --> 00:13:05.000
the reason you're ready to conquer the world

00:13:05.000 --> 00:13:07.000
is the environment supports what you're doing.

00:13:07.000 --> 00:13:10.000
And so I had to start to address my environment,

00:13:10.000 --> 00:13:12.000
and environment is the place you are,

00:13:12.000 --> 00:13:14.000
but most importantly in your environment

00:13:14.000 --> 00:13:16.000
is the people that are around you.

00:13:16.000 --> 00:13:18.000
Because write this down, number one,

00:13:18.000 --> 00:13:20.000
in our lives, the most powerful force

00:13:20.000 --> 00:13:21.000
that I'm aware of in the world

00:13:21.000 --> 00:13:23.000
is to be consistent and congruent

00:13:23.000 --> 00:13:25.000
with the expectations of our peer group.

00:13:25.000 --> 00:13:27.000
Let me say that to you again.

00:13:27.000 --> 00:13:29.000
The most powerful force on earth

00:13:29.000 --> 00:13:32.000
is we become consistent with the expectations

00:13:32.000 --> 00:13:33.000
of our peer group.

00:13:33.000 --> 00:13:35.000
You're going to get out of life

00:13:35.000 --> 00:13:37.000
what the people around you expect of you.

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:39.000
And so I had to begin to address

00:13:39.000 --> 00:13:40.000
who were the people around me,

00:13:40.000 --> 00:13:42.000
and specifically what was the environment that I was in.

00:13:42.000 --> 00:13:45.000
Because number two, proximity is power.

00:13:45.000 --> 00:13:46.000
The closer somebody is to you,

00:13:46.000 --> 00:13:48.000
the more influence they have over you.

00:13:48.000 --> 00:13:50.000
That's why your personal relationship that you're in

00:13:50.000 --> 00:13:53.000
is something that must be evaluated at all given times.

00:13:53.000 --> 00:13:55.000
And people ask me, how do I get more spouse support

00:13:55.000 --> 00:13:57.000
or partner support, boyfriend or girlfriend support?

00:13:57.000 --> 00:13:59.000
I don't know that you're always going to get more support,

00:13:59.000 --> 00:14:01.000
and I don't even know that that's needed.

00:14:01.000 --> 00:14:03.000
But one thing that's a foundation of all relationships

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:06.000
is does this person believe in me?

00:14:06.000 --> 00:14:07.000
Most people love us.

00:14:07.000 --> 00:14:08.000
That's one thing.

00:14:08.000 --> 00:14:09.000
If we're in a relationship,

00:14:09.000 --> 00:14:10.000
we kind of feel a level of love.

00:14:10.000 --> 00:14:13.000
But the deeper question is do they truly believe in me?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:16.000
And when I started to evaluate my friends

00:14:16.000 --> 00:14:17.000
that were around me,

00:14:17.000 --> 00:14:19.000
if I asked myself,

00:14:19.000 --> 00:14:21.000
were they supporting where I wanted to go in my life?

00:14:21.000 --> 00:14:23.000
Not that they didn't love me or like me.

00:14:23.000 --> 00:14:24.000
In fact, what most of us do

00:14:24.000 --> 00:14:27.000
is we love to have people around us who accept us.

00:14:27.000 --> 00:14:29.000
We say, I want people to accept me as I am.

00:14:29.000 --> 00:14:31.000
And there's a benefit to that.

00:14:31.000 --> 00:14:32.000
There's a huge negative as well.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:34.000
If people are constantly accepting this version of you,

00:14:34.000 --> 00:14:38.000
there's nothing compelling you to go to the next version.

00:14:38.000 --> 00:14:40.000
There's no stimulus that says I better change.

00:14:40.000 --> 00:14:41.000
There's no discomfort.

00:14:41.000 --> 00:14:43.000
Because these people closest to us,

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.000
their proximity has influence over us.

00:14:45.000 --> 00:14:47.000
So number one thing I want you to ask yourself

00:14:47.000 --> 00:14:49.000
is do the people around me believe in me?

00:14:49.000 --> 00:14:51.000
And if they don't, that needs to be evaluated.

00:14:51.000 --> 00:14:53.000
People say, well, then what do I do?

00:14:53.000 --> 00:14:54.000
Do I get rid of them?

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.000
Well, maybe, in some case.

00:14:55.000 --> 00:14:57.000
I mean, if they're antagonistic to you, certainly.

00:14:57.000 --> 00:15:00.000
But what you have to do is begin to add people

00:15:00.000 --> 00:15:02.000
in your proximity who do believe in you

00:15:02.000 --> 00:15:03.000
or who will believe in you.

00:15:03.000 --> 00:15:05.000
And if they don't believe in you,

00:15:05.000 --> 00:15:07.000
perhaps they don't need to be eliminated from your life,

00:15:07.000 --> 00:15:09.000
but one thing you may need to do

00:15:09.000 --> 00:15:11.000
is start to reduce their proximity to you.

00:15:11.000 --> 00:15:13.000
Maybe they're not as close to you as they used to be.

00:15:13.000 --> 00:15:15.000
I've had to do that many times in my life

00:15:15.000 --> 00:15:17.000
where I've had to eliminate a few people from my life,

00:15:17.000 --> 00:15:18.000
but very few.

00:15:18.000 --> 00:15:21.000
This is so critical to you becoming successful

00:15:21.000 --> 00:15:23.000
because your environmental gain

00:15:23.000 --> 00:15:26.000
is more important even than your mental gain

00:15:26.000 --> 00:15:27.000
because it's what supports it.

00:15:27.000 --> 00:15:29.000
And so I want you to evaluate a few things.

00:15:29.000 --> 00:15:30.000
Do they believe in me?

00:15:30.000 --> 00:15:34.000
Number two, are they a past or future reference type friend?

00:15:34.000 --> 00:15:36.000
In other words, when you're around them,

00:15:36.000 --> 00:15:39.000
what do you find yourself talking the most about?

00:15:39.000 --> 00:15:41.000
Is it the past or the future?

00:15:41.000 --> 00:15:44.000
I want to be around people who are constantly talking

00:15:44.000 --> 00:15:47.000
about either the present, but most importantly, the future.

00:15:47.000 --> 00:15:49.000
In other words, I want people who are present with me

00:15:49.000 --> 00:15:51.000
so that when they're with me, we're together.

00:15:51.000 --> 00:15:52.000
You know you have those friends too

00:15:52.000 --> 00:15:53.000
who are constantly not present

00:15:53.000 --> 00:15:55.000
even though they're in your presence.

00:15:55.000 --> 00:15:56.000
We don't want that either.

00:15:56.000 --> 00:15:58.000
But if people are constantly taking me

00:15:58.000 --> 00:16:00.000
in the past frame of reference,

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:03.000
old stories, old things, remember when,

00:16:03.000 --> 00:16:05.000
high school, college, previous date,

00:16:05.000 --> 00:16:08.000
previous vacation, previous business, remember when,

00:16:08.000 --> 00:16:11.000
constantly, you know, they're just always reminiscing.

00:16:11.000 --> 00:16:13.000
Or are they projecting me into the future?

00:16:13.000 --> 00:16:15.000
If at least 75% of your conversations

00:16:15.000 --> 00:16:18.000
aren't about the future with the people that you're around,

00:16:18.000 --> 00:16:21.000
these are not people supporting your future,

00:16:21.000 --> 00:16:23.000
they're supporting your past.

00:16:23.000 --> 00:16:25.000
They're reinforcing your past.

00:16:25.000 --> 00:16:26.000
The more we talk about something,

00:16:26.000 --> 00:16:29.000
the more we reinforce its importance in our life.

00:16:29.000 --> 00:16:31.000
And so this is a very subtle thing,

00:16:31.000 --> 00:16:33.000
and I think even as I say it, you're going, whoa,

00:16:33.000 --> 00:16:36.000
they do love me, I think they might believe in me,

00:16:36.000 --> 00:16:39.000
but man, we talk about the past all the time.

00:16:39.000 --> 00:16:41.000
Well, this is somebody who's going to reinforce

00:16:41.000 --> 00:16:42.000
that state of your life.

00:16:42.000 --> 00:16:45.000
You need to add people to your proximity

00:16:45.000 --> 00:16:47.000
who are discussing the future with you.

